{"id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard#lem:dc-ch7-2-8-normal-ball-dist","title":"lem:dc-ch7-2-8-normal-ball-dist","path":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard.md","line":275,"body":"","kind":"lemma","status":"not_started","tex":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard.tex#lem:dc-ch7-2-8-normal-ball-dist","uses":["[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard#def:dc-ch7-2-4]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#def:dc-ch3-expmap]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-2-9-c1diffeo]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-3-6-radius]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-3-6-reach]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-3-6-rayspeed]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard#lem:dc-ch7-2-8-gram-bound]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard#lem:dc-ch7-2-8-chart-length]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard.tex","label":"lem:dc-ch7-2-8-normal-ball-dist","line":465,"source":"\\begin{lemma}[the metric normal ball]\n\n  \\label{lem:dc-ch7-2-8-normal-ball-dist}\n\n  \\uses{def:dc-ch7-2-4, def:dc-ch3-expmap, lem:dc-ch3-2-9-c1diffeo, lem:dc-ch3-3-6-radius, lem:dc-ch3-3-6-reach, lem:dc-ch3-3-6-rayspeed, lem:dc-ch7-2-8-gram-bound, lem:dc-ch7-2-8-chart-length}\n\n  \\dcref{ch7:2.8}\nLet $M$ be a Riemannian manifold whose distance $d$ is the Riemannian\n  distance of \\cref{def:dc-ch7-2-4} and let $p\\in M$. There are\n  $\\varepsilon,\\delta>0$ such that $\\exp_p$ is injective and open on\n  $B_\\varepsilon(0)\\subset T_pM$ and:\n  \\begin{enumerate}\n  \\item (\\emph{radial geodesics realize the distance})\n    $d\\big(p,\\exp_p v\\big)=|v|_p$ for every $v$ with $\\|v\\|<\\varepsilon$;\n  \\item (\\emph{escape estimate}) $d(p,q)\\ge\\delta$ for every\n    $q\\notin\\exp_p\\big(B_\\varepsilon(0)\\big)$ -- the normal ball contains the\n    metric ball $B_\\delta(p)$.\n  \\end{enumerate}\n\\end{lemma}\n\\begin{proof}\n\n\n  \\uses{lem:dc-ch3-2-9-c1diffeo, lem:dc-ch3-3-6-radius, lem:dc-ch3-3-6-reach, lem:dc-ch3-3-6-rayspeed, lem:dc-ch7-2-8-gram-bound, lem:dc-ch7-2-8-chart-length}\n\\sketch The Gauss lemma and the local diffeomorphism properties of $\\exp_p$ give radial minimizing geodesics inside a sufficiently small normal ball. Compactness of the unit sphere and the chart length comparison give a positive lower bound for curves that leave this ball.\n\\end{proof}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Lemma</div></section>[the metric normal ball] <p></p><span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-6c656d3a64632d6368372d322d382d6e6f726d616c2d62616c6c2d64697374\"></span> <p></p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard%23def%3Adc-ch7-2-4\">↗ def:dc-ch7-2-4</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods%23def%3Adc-ch3-expmap\">↗ def:dc-ch3-expmap</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods%23lem%3Adc-ch3-2-9-c1diffeo\">↗ lem:dc-ch3-2-9-c1diffeo</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods%23lem%3Adc-ch3-3-6-radius\">↗ lem:dc-ch3-3-6-radius</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods%23lem%3Adc-ch3-3-6-reach\">↗ lem:dc-ch3-3-6-reach</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods%23lem%3Adc-ch3-3-6-rayspeed\">↗ lem:dc-ch3-3-6-rayspeed</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard%23lem%3Adc-ch7-2-8-gram-bound\">↗ lem:dc-ch7-2-8-gram-bound</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard%23lem%3Adc-ch7-2-8-chart-length\">↗ lem:dc-ch7-2-8-chart-length</a> <p></p><span class=\"tex-source-references\" role=\"list\" style=\"display:block\"><span class=\"tex-dcref\" role=\"listitem\" style=\"display:block\">1. ch7:2.8</span></span>Let <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$M$\">$M$</span> be a Riemannian manifold whose distance <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$d$\">$d$</span> is the Riemannian distance of <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard%23def%3Adc-ch7-2-4\" data-tex-node=\"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard#def:dc-ch7-2-4\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-6465663a64632d6368372d322d34\">section 1</a> and let <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$p\\in M$\">$p\\in M$</span>. There are <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\varepsilon ,\\delta &gt;0$\">$\\varepsilon ,\\delta &gt;0$</span> such that <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\exp _p$\">$\\exp _p$</span> is injective and open on <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$B_\\varepsilon (0)\\subset T_pM$\">$B_\\varepsilon (0)\\subset T_pM$</span> and: <ol><li><p>(<em>radial geodesics realize the distance</em>) <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$d\\big(p,\\exp _p v\\big)=|v|_p$\">$d\\big(p,\\exp _p v\\big)=|v|_p$</span> for every <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$v$\">$v$</span> with <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\| v\\| &lt;\\varepsilon $\">$\\| v\\| &lt;\\varepsilon $</span>; </p></li><li><p>(<em>escape estimate</em>) <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$d(p,q)\\ge \\delta $\">$d(p,q)\\ge \\delta $</span> for every <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$q\\notin \\exp _p\\big(B_\\varepsilon (0)\\big)$\">$q\\notin \\exp _p\\big(B_\\varepsilon (0)\\big)$</span> – the normal ball contains the metric ball <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$B_\\delta (p)$\">$B_\\delta (p)$</span>. </p></li></ol>  <section class=\"theorem proof\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proof</div><p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods%23lem%3Adc-ch3-2-9-c1diffeo\">↗ lem:dc-ch3-2-9-c1diffeo</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods%23lem%3Adc-ch3-3-6-radius\">↗ lem:dc-ch3-3-6-radius</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods%23lem%3Adc-ch3-3-6-reach\">↗ lem:dc-ch3-3-6-reach</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods%23lem%3Adc-ch3-3-6-rayspeed\">↗ lem:dc-ch3-3-6-rayspeed</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard%23lem%3Adc-ch7-2-8-gram-bound\">↗ lem:dc-ch7-2-8-gram-bound</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard%23lem%3Adc-ch7-2-8-chart-length\">↗ lem:dc-ch7-2-8-chart-length</a> \\sketch The Gauss lemma and the local diffeomorphism properties of <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\exp _p$\">$\\exp _p$</span> give radial minimizing geodesics inside a sufficiently small normal ball. Compactness of the unit sphere and the chart length comparison give a positive lower bound for curves that leave this ball. </p><span class=\"qed\" aria-label=\"证毕\" style=\"display:block;text-align:right\">□</span></section>","warnings":["部分 TeX 排版细节未完整还原（已保留可读内容）: sketch"]},"previous":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard#lem:dc-ch7-2-8-chart-length","next":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard#lem:dc-ch7-2-8-ray-geodesic","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard#def:dc-ch7-2-4","title":"def:dc-ch7-2-4","label":"def:dc-ch7-2-4"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#def:dc-ch3-expmap","title":"def:dc-ch3-expmap","label":"def:dc-ch3-expmap"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-2-9-c1diffeo","title":"lem:dc-ch3-2-9-c1diffeo","label":"lem:dc-ch3-2-9-c1diffeo"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-3-6-radius","title":"lem:dc-ch3-3-6-radius","label":"lem:dc-ch3-3-6-radius"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-3-6-reach","title":"lem:dc-ch3-3-6-reach","label":"lem:dc-ch3-3-6-reach"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-3-6-rayspeed","title":"lem:dc-ch3-3-6-rayspeed","label":"lem:dc-ch3-3-6-rayspeed"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard#lem:dc-