-bound, lem:dc-ch7-2-8-chart-length}\n\\sketch The Gauss lemma and the local diffeomorphism properties of $\\exp_p$ give radial minimizing geodesics inside a sufficiently small normal ball. Compactness of the unit sphere and the chart length comparison give a positive lower bound for curves that leave this ball.\n\\end{proof}","source":"tex/references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard.tex","description":"","dependencies":[{"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard#def:dc-ch7-2-4","title":"def:dc-ch7-2-4","description":""},{"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#def:dc-ch3-expmap","title":"def:dc-ch3-expmap","description":""},{"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-2-9-c1diffeo","title":"lem:dc-ch3-2-9-c1diffeo","description":""},{"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-3-6-radius","title":"lem:dc-ch3-3-6-radius","description":""},{"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-3-6-reach","title":"lem:dc-ch3-3-6-reach","description":""},{"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-3-6-rayspeed","title":"lem:dc-ch3-3-6-rayspeed","description":""},{"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard#lem:dc-ch7-2-8-gram-bound","title":"lem:dc-ch7-2-8-gram-bound","description":""},{"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_CompleteManifoldsHopfRinowHadamard#lem:dc-ch7-2-8-chart-length","title":"lem:dc-ch7-2-8-chart-length","description":""}],"dependencies_omitted":0,"unresolved_dependencies":[],"unresolved_omitted":0}}